//
// Library.SymbolTable.ailang
// OS-agnostic symbol table manager.
// Location: Librarys/Compiler/Link/Core/Library.SymbolTable.ailang
// Import:   LibraryImport.Compiler.Link.Core.SymbolTable
//
// PURPOSE:
//   Tracks symbols during codegen across three bindings:
//     LOCAL  — file-internal (STB_LOCAL),     e.g. static helpers.
//     GLOBAL — defined and exported (STB_GLOBAL, st_shndx != 0),
//              e.g. ail_main, ail_exit for a kernel module.
//     UND    — global but undefined (STB_GLOBAL, st_shndx == SHN_UNDEF),
//              e.g. ail_printk referenced by a payload.
//
// STRICT ORDERING (ELF requirement):
//   All LOCALs first, then GLOBALs (defined or undefined).
//   The symtab section's sh_info MUST equal the count of LOCAL symbols
//   (= index of first non-local). Getting this wrong -> `ld` rejects the object.
//
// REQUIRED EXPORTS (API sketch):
//   SymTable_AddLocal(name, section_idx, offset)
//   SymTable_AddGlobalDefined(name, section_idx, offset)
//   SymTable_AddUndefined(name)
//   SymTable_FirstNonLocal()   -> value for sh_info
//   SymTable_ResolveNameToIdx(name) -> sym_idx for reloc records
//   SymTable_EmitBytes(buf)    -> writes Elf64_Sym array + strtab
//
// STATUS: Scaffold. Existing CELFBuilder already has minimal symtab
// code that emits only file + section symbols; lift and generalize here.
